# Domains blocked while AI lockout is active.
# One domain per line, blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Edit this file, then re-run ai-domain-block-install.sh (with sudo) to
# apply changes - the enforcement script only trusts the root-owned copy
# it installs to /etc/omarchy-ai-lockout/domains.list, not this source file,
# so edits here don't take effect until you reinstall.
#
# Note: github.com/copilot can't be listed here - it's a path on github.com,
# not its own domain, and blocking github.com would break all of GitHub.
# However, GitHub Copilot's actual completions/chat backend runs on separate
# hostnames (per GitHub's own allowlist docs), so blocking those below
# breaks Copilot's functionality even though the github.com/copilot page
# itself still loads.
chatgpt.com
www.chatgpt.com
chat.openai.com
claude.ai
gemini.google.com
copilot.microsoft.com
perplexity.ai
www.perplexity.ai
githubcopilot.com
api.githubcopilot.com
api.individual.githubcopilot.com
api.business.githubcopilot.com
api.enterprise.githubcopilot.com
copilot-proxy.githubusercontent.com
origin-tracker.githubusercontent.com
copilot-telemetry.githubusercontent.com
default.exp-tas.com
